[Music]  2005 Shadow of the Colossus was a  revelation a game whose gorgeous  aesthetic and reserved tone were at the  time undeniably distinct together with  its unique take on boss encounters and a  stirring soundtrack it was a defining  title of the PlayStation 2 euro but it  was also a game infamous for its  technical issues most notably it's  choppy aggravating framerate a 2011 HD  remaster for the ps3 alleviated the  title of this significant tarnish and  now with 2018 shut up the Colossus for  PlayStation 4 Blue Point games have  completely rebuilt every aspect of the  games world while leaving its underlying  structure and mechanics intact a move  which not only enhances the game  visually but uncatted godly intensifies  the utter majesty of this extraordinary  experience  for those unfamiliar Shadow of the  Colossus takes place in an ancient world  where young warrior Wanda and his horse  augur transport a deceased loved one to  a forbidden sealed land armed with only  a sword and bow wander hopes to take  advantage of a fable that suggests that  something in this isolated province has  the means to bring back the dead there  he encounters an omnipresent entity who  compels him to destroy 16 colossi hidden  throughout the territory in order to  enable his wish if you've already played  a previous version of Shadow of the  Colossus you'll find that blue points  where Nishan feels much the same barring  some minor differences in controller  mapping some subtle quality of life  tweaks and a new easter egg the  locations of each Colossus and their  method of defeat remain the same as do  the locations of every white-tailed  lizard and fruit collectible the weight  and movement physics of Wanda and Argo  feel unchanged and new game+ rewards are  identical but the impact of this  completely rebuilt world is transcendent  this is a world that is geographically  as you remember but one that constantly  astounds you as if seeing it for the  first time highly detailed environment  modeling in tandem with impressive light  and shadow simulation bring amazing life  to the game's breathtaking biomes  luscious forests are densely packed with  majestically tall trees and twisting  foliage dappled beautifully with soft  rays of sunlight vast arid deserts feel  horribly desolate as you try and sight  somber ruins through a wispy sandstorm  even the simple side of mountainous  crags and cliff faces is impressive with  shadows acutely defining their rocky  surfaces making them pop ominously every  place you travel to in this world every  time you crest a hill emerge from a  crevasse or change or perspective the  landscape will be a sight worthy of  pores  the increased fidelity of the  reconstruction colossi is just as  spectacular and the mere sight of one in  this version of the game is even more  inspiring than it is in your memory each  fo some small and nimble the rest  impossibly Titanic and overbearing is a  terrifying beast of stone fur and  leather that fur is now noticed ly more  dense and luscious and hanging onto it  for dear life as your enemy tries to  violently shake you off feels even more  intense these moments are enhanced by  the increased fidelity of the  environment that lies far beneath you  went on top of a colossus combined with  motion effects which amplify the sense  of danger at these dizzying heights the  first time I mounted a flying claws in  this version of the game I could feel my  chest wrench as I answer Slee squeeze my  controllers to hold onto its wing for  dear life while it soared and flat  wildly through the air  it was truly exhilarating playing on a  ps4 Pro offers you the ability to  further enhance visual fidelity by a  high dynamic range color as well as the  choice between two different graphical  options with different priorities  cinematic mode enables 4k resolutions on  4k screens as well as allowing for  impressive down sampling for 1080  displays at a targeted 30fps performance  mode provides less impressive graphical  quality but maintains a smoother  framerate targeting 60fps in my  experience I prefer the crisper image  offered in cinematic mode once you  realize that you can recognize the  definition between each individual blade  of grass it's hard to let that go  however the visual quality offered by  both modes still enhances the experience  of the game in ways previously mentioned  especially for those whose last memory  of it was suffering through subsidy  Affairs framerate issues on the original  ps2 release  [Music]  it is so fortunate that this visual  reconstruction doesn't detract from what  makes shout of the Colossus a great  achievement the game's holistic and  understated direction still comes  through incredibly it's muted colors  cinematic camera angles and a stock  absence of music while exploring the  world still evokes a poignant tone of  desolation and solitude the walls large  forsaken landscape doesn't feel bereft  of things to do because simply riding  through it and enjoying the majesty of  the land accompanied only by the sound  of augo's hooves scraping against the  earth it's a delightfully meditative  experience fighting a colossus is still  a grand solemn and tense challenge that  is exhilarating to overcome the  impassioned orchestral soundtrack  heightens the pressure of every maneuver  working out how to mount the impossibly  enormous enemy clambering to reach their  vulnerabilities as they try to fling you  off and driving a sword into their flesh  every moment of a colossus battle is  thrilling to execute and witness whether  you're doing it for the first time or  the 15th time in a postgame Time Trial  while the passing of 12 years hasn't  affected the overall quality of Shadow  of the Colossus there are two technical  annoyances that persist and remind you  of a bygone era the third-person camera  system doesn't clip through world  objects so it becomes erratic and  troublesome to adjust when moving  through enclosed spaces or near a solid  object  additionally the game's unforgiving  climbing system which asks you to jump  with the X button and grasp onto a ledge  or surface with the r2 trigger is  occasionally temperamental there may be  times when contact with the ledge may  not correctly register even though you  may have been holding on to well in  advance and correctly estimated your  distance needed for the jump however  both of these issues affect only a small  amount of time of the game and should  not be considered a significant strike  in the case of the climbing system it's  a quirk which is easy to come to peace  with because of how absolutely essential  the mechanic is to creating the rousing  pressure and suspense of Colossus and  counties  Shadow of the Colossus is a tremendous  journey and one well worth taking and  retaking the visual level hole is simply  stunning and thoroughly enhances every  facet of wonder and Nagas excellent  adventure galloping through the wealth  is always breathtaking and felling a  monumental Colossus is always humbling  Shadow of the Colossus is a beautiful  reconstruction of an already exceptional  title it continues to be a modern  classic and is an extraordinary game  that everyone must experience

